/*
Skinfamilies are for the stages of damage. Only useful for when you want to keep the gibbing system or keep the burning texture.
The amount of skingroups and order MUST REMAIN THE SAME!
The order is always Default, Wounded, Burning, Wounded+Burning. then the order repeats for a different set of materials.

L4D1 CI usually don't have the burning material, but the order of "Default, Wounded, Burning, Wounded+Burning" is still there.
If you only want burned body materials without wounds (cause the cutout system sucks), just do "Default, Default, Burning, Burning" instead.
If you don't want any wounds or burning, you could just not have any texturegroups at all

Also, if you are using skingroups, every material on your model bust be in each texturegroup line.

Extra note:
Some L4D1 CI have really stupid texture groups. 
"Male_Suit.mdl" for example lists "common_male_black_head_03_wounded" a whole awful lot of times for no apparent reason.
I don't know if they have any use. But you probably should replace all of those with any other dud material that doesn't actually do anything. 
Its just some ugly jank TLS did for *some* reason.
*/

$TextureGroup "skinfamilies"
{
	{ "common_female_suit_head_01"         "common_female_shorthair_head_01"         "common_female_suit_upper_01"         "common_female_suit_lower_01"         "common_female_suit_head_01_wounded" "common_female_shorthair_head_01_wounded" "common_female_suit_upper_01_wounded" "common_female_suit_lower_01_wounded" "common_female_suit_head_02" "common_female_shorthair_head_02" "common_female_suit_head_02_wounded" "common_female_shorthair_head_02_wounded" "common_female_suit_head_03" "common_female_shorthair_head_03" "common_female_suit_head_03_wounded" "common_female_shorthair_head_03_wounded" "common_female_suit_upper_02" "common_female_suit_upper_02_wounded" "common_female_suit_upper_03" "common_female_suit_upper_03_wounded" "common_female_suit_upper_04" "common_female_suit_upper_04_wounded" "common_female_suit_upper_05" "common_female_suit_upper_05_wounded" "common_female_suit_lower_02" "common_female_suit_lower_02_wounded" "common_female_suit_lower_03" "common_female_suit_lower_03_wounded" "common_female_suit_lower_04" "common_female_suit_lower_04_wounded" }
